-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Numerical Instability:** The estimated alpha $\alpha$ must be clipped to $[10^{-6}, 1 - 10^{-6}]$ before computing the logarithm in the mask loss to avoid `NaN` values [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Color Space:** Colors must be gamma-corrected back to linear intensity before computing the L1 color loss [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Flow Scale:** Optical flow is measured in the scale of half the shorter image dimension, which influences the choice of $\lambda_F$ [S1, unofficial].
+**Pitfalls:**
+*   **Numerical Instability:** Failing to clip $\hat{\alpha}$ before computing $\log(\hat{\alpha})$ or $\log(1-\hat{\alpha})$ leads to NaN gradients [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Flow Scale:** Optical flow should be measured in the scale of half the shorter image dimension to ensure appropriate weighting relative to color loss [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Gamma Correction:** Colors should be gamma-corrected back to linear intensity before computing L1 loss [S1, unofficial].
 
